# Keep the build context to the source that actually goes in the image.
#
# Without this, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile takes everything: the caches and
# rendered frames under outputs/, the benchmark upload zip, the git history,
# and, worst of all, the .env holding the API key, which would then sit
# inside any image that got shared.

# secrets: never inside an image
.env
*.key
**/_key_do_not_share.csv

# generated results; the container writes these to a mounted volume instead
outputs/
outputs_base/

# the benchmark upload artefacts (~90 MB) are built by a script when needed
datasets/

# the dataset is mounted at /data, never baked in (CC-BY, ~1 GB)
SpatialAwareRobotDataset*/
extended_raw_data/

# local environments and caches
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# version control and editor state
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/

# generated LaTeX tree and its zip; the Markdown chapters are the source
dissertation/latex/
dissertation/latex.zip

# demo media kept out of the repo and out of the image
*.mp4
*.gif
